

## Deploy to Vercel

This project exports the Express app for Vercel and keeps `npm start` for local use.

### Deploy using the Vercel CLI (Windows PowerShell)

From the project folder:

```powershell
npm install
npm start
```

Stop the local server with `Ctrl+C`, then run:

```powershell
npx vercel
```

Follow the prompts to log in and create/link a Vercel project. For a preview deployment, accept the defaults. When it finishes, open the URL printed by Vercel.

Deploy to production with:

```powershell
npx vercel --prod
```

The `public` directory contains the static frontend assets. Vercel serves those files and runs the exported Express app for the backend routes.

